mode: "100644"
text: "# Examples — discoverability sets in practice\n\nWorked examples showing the **keyword/SEO layer first**, then a tight tag set per platform, plus a\nbranded-tag design — and a contrast with the old 30-tag block. Topic: a SaaS founder's post about\ndeleting their most-requested feature. Adapt tags to the real account/niche; always vet on-platform.\n\n---\n\n## Example 1 — Instagram Reel (hard cap 5)\n\n**Keyword/SEO layer (the real lever):**\n- **Caption (front-loaded):** \"Why we deleted our most-requested SaaS feature — and what we built\n  instead.\" (primary keyword: *SaaS feature* / *product decisions*)\n- **On-screen text:** \"We deleted our #1 requested feature.\"\n- **Spoken:** say \"most-requested feature\" and \"product decisions\" aloud.\n- **Audio:** a relevant trending sound (does more than tags for Reels reach).\n\n**Hashtags (3–5, niche/mid-tier, in caption):**\n`#BuildInPublic #SaaSProduct #ProductManagement #StartupLessons #IndieHackers`\n*(branded tag optional, e.g. `#WoopBuildLog`)*\n\n→ 5 tags, all relevant, mid-tier, no generic mega-tags. Respects the IG cap.\n\n---\n\n## Example 2 — TikTok (treat tags as keywords)\n\n**Triple-mention keyword:** \"delete a feature\" / \"SaaS product decisions\" — **spoken + on-screen +\ncaption front**.\n**Caption:** \"How we decide what to build for our SaaS (we deleted our most-requested feature).\"\n**Hashtags (3–5, as keywords, 1 broad + niche):**\n`#SaaS #BuildInPublic #StartupTok #ProductDecisions #FoundersOfTikTok`\n\n→ `#StartupTok`/`#FoundersOfTikTok` signal the right side of TikTok; no `#fyp`. The keywords, not the\ntags, do the ranking.\n\n---\n\n## Example 3 — LinkedIn (3–5 specific)\n\n**Keywords** live in the post body naturally (LinkedIn indexes them).\n**Hashtags:** `#SaaS #ProductManagement #BuildInPublic` — specific, not `#Leadership`/`#Business`.\n\n## Example 4 — X / Twitter\n\n**0–1 tag.** The post carries itself; add a single tag only to join a live conversation. Usually\nnone.\n\n---\n\n## Example 5 — a branded/campaign hashtag\n\n**Branded (ongoing):** `#WoopBuildLog` — short, unique, on-brand; goes in the bio + every build-log\npost; followers use it to share their own build updates.\n**Campaign (time-bound):** `#WoopLaunchWeek` — for a launch; promoted in the CTA (\"post your setup\nwith #WoopLaunchWeek\"); tracked via native search.\n*(Both checked first to confirm they're unused and typo-safe.)*\n\n---\n\n## Contrast — the old block (do NOT do this)\n\n`#love #viral #fyp #explore #instagood #follow4follow #marketing #business #entrepreneur\n#success #motivation #socialmedia #digitalmarketing #growth #contentcreator …(×30)`\n\n→ Generic mega-tags that bury the post; `#fyp` does nothing; over the IG cap; identical on every\npost; zero relevance signal. If a user asks for this, redirect to a tight relevant set + the keyword\nlayer.\n\n---\n\n## What the good examples share\n\n- **Keywords/SEO done first** (caption front + on-screen + spoken), because that drives discovery.\n- A **tight, relevant, mid-tier** tag set, **per platform**, within caps.\n- **No generic mega-tags**, no `#fyp`, no 30-tag block.\n- A **branded tag** where community/UGC applies.\n- Honest framing: tags categorize and aid search; content + engagement drive reach.\n"
